// Retouch heal, step 1 — packs the tone/color DIFFERENCE between the destination and the source over the ring.
//
// Output: rgb = (destination - source) * ringWeight, alpha = ringWeight. One Gaussian blur of this image then
// blurs numerator (rgb) and denominator (alpha) together, and `RetouchHealCombine` divides them — "normalised
// convolution": a smooth membrane that equals the ring's average difference near the ring and interpolates
// across the hole. Signed values (the difference can be negative) are fine: the pipeline works in float.
// MEASURED (spot-removal spike, docs/ROADMAP_HISTORY.md): this recipe runs in the PERCEPTUAL domain; in linear it
// leaves pale halos (rock-large halo error 0.0379 linear vs 0.0165 perceptual).
kernel vec4 retouchHealDiff(__sample dst, __sample src, __sample geo) {
    return vec4((dst.rgb - src.rgb) * geo.g, geo.g);
}
